# Package-local clang-format configuration.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The repository has no top-level .clang-format, so
# `clang-format --style=file` run from inside this package falls back to the
# LLVM defaults, whose PointerAlignment is Right. That rewrites
#
#   OpaqueCreated* PKG_00C12310_THISCALL create_cached_object_00c12310(
#
# into
#
#   OpaqueCreated *PKG_00C12310_THISCALL create_cached_object_00c12310(
#
# and the second form is invisible to validate.RETURN_DECL, whose return-type
# run is `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:<>*&]*` followed by an optional all-caps
# convention token and then the symbol name. With the `*` detached from the
# return type the convention token no longer parses as a convention, the name no
# longer parses as a name, and the target span -- the one the whole validation
# reads -- cannot be bound at all. `_target_span` then finds no span and every
# dimension reports NOT_AVAILABLE for a source that is correct.
#
# So the pointer alignment is pinned to Left here, which keeps the `*` inside the
# return-type run and keeps the declaration readable by the checker. The rest
# follows AGENTS.md's stated style: a modified Google.
#
# This file is scoped to this package directory. It changes no other package and
# no other file in the repository.
BasedOnStyle: Google
PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
ColumnLimit: 80
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
